# =============================================================================
# Trivy ignore list — accepted base-image vulnerabilities
# =============================================================================
# The relay and ui images share the python:3.12-slim-trixie (Debian 13) base.
# List here only CVEs that cannot be fixed by patching, `apt-get upgrade` or a
# newer base-image digest, or that do not apply to these images. Each one is
# accepted as documented risk — see the "Known Accepted Risks" section in
# SECURITY.md for the full rationale.
#
# This file is auto-loaded by Trivy from the repository root, so the scan in
# .github/workflows/security-scan.yml (which fails on fixable HIGH/CRITICAL
# findings) passes with the acceptance recorded in version control.
# Re-review when fixes ship and drop resolved entries.
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-11-27
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The move to Debian 13 cleared the four entries that were listed for Debian 12
# (CVE-2023-45853 zlib, CVE-2026-8376 and CVE-2026-42496 perl-base,
# CVE-2025-7458 libsqlite3).
#
# Entries may carry an expiry date (`exp:YYYY-MM-DD`): after it Trivy reports
# the CVE again, which forces a new review instead of a permanent ignore.

# setuptools 70.3.0 (ui and relay images) — not installed as a package. pip
# vendors only `pkg_resources` from setuptools 70.3.0 and lists that version in
# pip/_vendor/vendor.txt, which is what Trivy reports. The vulnerable code is
# not shipped: CVE-2025-47273 (HIGH) is in setuptools' PackageIndex.download,
# CVE-2026-59890 (MEDIUM) in its sdist MANIFEST.in handling, and
# GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w (LOW) in legacy wheel installs on Windows. None of that
# code is in the image, and nothing is built or installed at runtime. Drop
# these lines once pip vendors a fixed setuptools (84.1.0 or later).
CVE-2025-47273 exp:2027-05-31
CVE-2026-59890 exp:2027-05-31
GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w exp:2027-05-31
